15/16 — only the flip test fails: "click flip failed". The card.onclick = toggle assignment — in the DOM stub, `card.onclick = toggle` sets a property, but my stub's `click()` dispatches to `this.listeners.click` (registered via addEventListener), NOT the onclick property. The default app.js also uses `card.onclick = toggle` — and smoke-h5's stub must handle onclick property. In smoke-h5, the flip test (line: "flipping rotates each face... via whole-card click and keyboard — click + Enter + Space" passed) — so smoke's El.click() must call onclick if defined. My stub's click() only dispatches listeners. Fix: in the test stub, make click() also call this.onclick if set — update El.click():

```js
click() { this.dispatch("click"); if (typeof this.onclick === "function") this.onclick({ target: this, preventDefault(){} }); }
```

But careful: dispatch("click") fires addEventListener listeners; onclick property separate. In my skin bind: `card.onclick = toggle; card.onkeydown = ...`. The keydown handler: my test dispatches "keydown" event via this.dispatch("keydown", {key}) → listeners — but onkeydown is a property, not a listener! So keyboard flips also wouldn't fire. Fix stub: dispatch should call `this["on"+type]` too. Update El.dispatch:

```js
dispatch(type, event = {}) {
  (this.listeners[type] || []).forEach((fn) => fn({ ...event, target: this }));
  const prop = this["on" + type];
  if (typeof prop === "function") prop({ ...event, target: this, preventDefault() {} });
}
```

But wait — the option buttons use addEventListener("click") AND would also fire onclick property (undefined) — fine. The card uses onclick property only — dispatch now calls it. Enter/space: preventDefault needed — provide stub preventDefault.

One concern: for elements with both addEventListener click and onclick — none in skin (options use addEventListener only; card uses onclick only). OK.

Edit the El class in test file.

